          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#EveryPresheafIsAColimitOfRepresentables"} Every presheaf is a colimit of representables
              %li
                %a{:href => "#MacLanesCoYonedaLemma"} MacLane’s co-Yoneda lemma
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What is sometimes called the
            %em co-Yoneda lemma
            or
            %em density formula
            is a basic fact about
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            (a basic fact of
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representables
            and more precisely that it is the “colimit over itself of all the representables contained in it”.
          %p
            One might think of this as related by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} duality
            to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
          %h2#EveryPresheafIsAColimitOfRepresentables Every presheaf is a colimit of representables
          %p Throughout, let
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
                (for instance
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo =
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V =
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                with its
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Obj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒱
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c,d \in Obj(\mathcal{V})
            two objects, we write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}(c,d) \in V
            for the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+reduction"}> Yoneda reduction
                )
            %p
              Recall that the (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+Yoneda+lemma"}> enriched
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              says that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon \mathcal{C}^{op} \to V
              a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched functor
              out of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in \mathcal{C}
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [\mathcal{C}^{op},V]
                    \\big(
                    \\mathcal{C}(-,c)
                    ,\,
                    F
                    \\big)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    F(c)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where on the left we have the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+category"} enriched functor category
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} functor represented
              by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              and the given functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %p
              Using the expression of these hom-objects on the left as
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ends"} ends
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒞
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\int_{c' \in \mathcal{C}}
                    V\big(
                    \\mathcal{C}(c',c)
                    ,\, F(c')
                    \\big)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    F(c)
                    \\,.
            %p
              In this form the Yoneda lemma is also referred to as
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+reduction"} Yoneda reduction
          %p
            Under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} abstract duality
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end"} end
            turns into a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coend"} coend
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(c)
            in terms of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coend"} coend
          %p The natural candidate is the statement that:
          #coYonedaLemma.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representables
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F(c) \simeq \int^{c' \in C} \mathcal{C}(c,c')\otimes F(c')
            %p hence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒞
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F(-) \simeq \int^{c' \in \mathcal{C}} Y(c')\otimes F(c')
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              denotes the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
              = succeed "-language," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+functors"} tensor product of functors
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
